course: dictionary
lesson: 680
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so you need its context to know which one fits. Read the words around it and ask which meaning makes sense. «A hot-air balloon rises because a burner heats the air inside it» tells you a balloon here is a big craft with a basket that carries people.
explain: «Fishing line, hooks, released balloons and plastic drink rings can tangle animals.» Here a balloon is the thin rubber bag filled with air or gas. The words released and tangle help you see it is an object, not a flying machine.
explain: «To balloon» is a verb, an action word. It means to grow bigger very fast. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: if the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: A balloon is a thin rubber bag that you fill with air or gas.
fact: A balloon filled with helium floats.
fact: A hot-air balloon is a very big balloon with a basket that can carry people through the sky.
fact: «To balloon» means to grow bigger very fast.
fact: Helium atoms slip slowly through rubber, so «a helium balloon shrinks in a few days».
exercise: «Fishing line, hooks, released balloons and plastic drink rings can tangle animals.» In this sentence, what is a balloon? | *A thin rubber bag filled with air or gas | A very big basket that carries people | To grow bigger very fast
exercise: «A hot-air balloon rises because a burner heats the air inside it.» What does a hot-air balloon carry? | Sand from the beach | Water from the river to the town | *People, in a basket through the sky
exercise: Ben says, «My savings will balloon this year.» What does balloon mean here? | *To grow bigger very fast | To pop with a loud bang | To float slowly down to the ground | A thin rubber bag
test: «A piece of sticky tape on a balloon can let a pin go in without a bang.» Which meaning of balloon fits this sentence? | *A thin rubber bag filled with air or gas | To grow bigger very fast | A hot-air balloon with a basket
test: Which gas makes a balloon float, according to the fact box? | Pin | *Helium | Tape | Rubber
exam: In «To balloon is to grow bigger very fast», what kind of word is balloon? | *Verb | Adverb | Noun | Adjective
